  "explanation": "Document D2 explicitly states in segment S4 that 'Friedrich Kethorn... held the reins of power as the head of government of County of Bentheim.' This is a direct, unambiguous assertion matching the question's subject and relation. Document D1 describes 'Marius-Gabriel Gheorghiță' as a mysterious figure with an 'air of authority' who took a seat at a table in the town hall, but it does not explicitly state he holds the title of 'head of government.' The text in D1 is narrative fiction implying influence rather than stating an official office. Therefore, only Friedrich Kethorn is supported by a direct textual assertion for the specific role requested. The previous inclusion of Gheorghiță (R5) appears to be an over-interpretation of narrative description as a factual title claim."
